Here is the root cause:
The bug was caused by the introduction of a DT-based irqchip driver for the Marvell Kirkwood and Dove SoCs, which replaced the existing ASM interrupt handler used by non-DT boards. When both non-DT and DT support were enabled, selecting `MULTI_IRQ_HANDLER` led to a conflict, breaking the ASM irq handler for non-DT boards and resulting in improper interrupt handling.

